/-!
# Finite image-subalgebra models in integral ring diagrams

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 05N9 and 00GM, with the image-subalgebra
refinement in the DAG proof (blueprint: lem-sfb-noetherian-integral-colimit-image-model).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Algebra

/-- A finite algebra over a Noetherian colimit has a finite image-subalgebra model
at a stage of a compatible integral diagram.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 05N9, proof of (1), and Tag 00GM;
the image-subalgebra refinement is the agent-written proof of
(blueprint: lem-sfb-noetherian-integral-colimit-image-model).

The algebra structures on the stages encode the homomorphisms S_i to D_i.
`htransition` says their transition squares commute. The structures on the
coefficient colimit are specified by `hcoeff`; `hcompatible` specifies the
induced algebra structure on the second colimit. The tensor uses the right
factor's algebra structure, so it is literally H tensor S, as in the source.
The formula on every pure tensor identifies the equivalence with the canonical
multiplication map, rather than asserting only an unspecified isomorphism.

Proof:
1. Finite module generators give finite type. Since S is Noetherian,
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-noetherian-finite-presentation` gives a finite
   presentation of D (`def-weil-pbc-finitely-presented-algebra`).
2. Use `lem-pc-filtered-colimit-commrings-elementwise` (1) in each diagram
   to lift the presentation generators and the finitely many relation coefficients.
   Directedness puts all lifts at one stage; use nonemptiness for an empty list.
3. Each lifted relation evaluates to zero in D. Clause (2) of that same
   elementwise colimit lemma makes all these evaluations zero at a common later
   stage, using directedness finitely many times. With no relations retain the stage.
4. Let H be the subalgebra generated by the lifted generators in D_i. Integrality
   and `lem-sc-finite-generated-integral-subring` show it is a finite S_i-module.
   Its inclusion is injective even when S_i to D_i is not, so the relations hold in H.
5. The tensor pushout universal property
   (`lem-weil-pbc-algebra-tensor-pushout-universal-property`) gives multiplication
   H tensor S to D. Evaluate the chosen polynomial presentation in H tensor S
   at x_a tensor 1. Balancing moves each lifted coefficient across the tensor,
   so the relations vanish and evaluation descends to a map D to H tensor S.
6. The composite on D fixes coefficients and presentation generators. For the
   other composite, write h in H as a polynomial in the x_a. Balancing gives
   psi(h-bar) = h tensor 1, hence the composite fixes h tensor s for every h,s.
   Pure tensors generate (`def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product`), so the maps are
   inverse as S-algebra maps, with exactly the displayed pure-tensor formula.
-/
theorem exists_finite_subalgebra_colimit_model
    {I : Type u} [PartialOrder I] [Nonempty I] [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)]
    (S D : I ⥤ CommRingCat.{u})
    (cS : Cocone S) (hS : IsColimit cS) (cD : Cocone D) (hD : IsColimit cD)
    [∀ i : I, Algebra (S.obj i) (D.obj i)]
    [∀ i : I, Algebra (S.obj i) cS.pt] [Algebra cS.pt cD.pt]
    (htransition : ∀ (i j : I) (h : i ≤ j),
      (D.map (homOfLE h)).hom.comp (algebraMap (S.obj i) (D.obj i)) =
        (algebraMap (S.obj j) (D.obj j)).comp (S.map (homOfLE h)).hom)
    (hcoeff : ∀ i : I, algebraMap (S.obj i) cS.pt = (cS.ι.app i).hom)
    (hcompatible : ∀ i : I,
      (cD.ι.app i).hom.comp (algebraMap (S.obj i) (D.obj i)) =
        (algebraMap cS.pt cD.pt).comp (cS.ι.app i).hom)
    (hintegral : ∀ (i : I) (x : D.obj i), IsIntegral (S.obj i) x)
    [IsNoetherianRing cS.pt] [Module.Finite cS.pt cD.pt] :
    ∃ (i : I) (H : Subalgebra (S.obj i) (D.obj i)), Module.Finite (S.obj i) H ∧
      ∃ e : @AlgEquiv cS.pt (H ⊗[S.obj i] cS.pt) cD.pt _ _ _
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra (R := S.obj i) (A := H) (B := cS.pt)) _,
        ∀ (h : H) (s : cS.pt),
          e (h ⊗ₜ[S.obj i] s) =
            (@_root_.id cD.pt ((cD.ι.app i).hom (h : D.obj i))) * algebraMap cS.pt cD.pt s := by
  sorry

end Algebra
